quran[17]{c,v,t}:
  52,15,"Is this magic, or is it you who do not see?"
  52,16,"Enter it (and burn): whether you are patient or impatient, it will be the same for you. You are only being rewarded for what you used to do.’"
  52,17,"Indeed, the God-conscious will be in the Gardens and Bliss,"
  52,18,rejoicing in whatever their Lord has granted them. And their Lord has saved them from the punishment of Hell.
  52,19,(They will be told:) ‘Enjoy your food and drink as a reward for what you used to do.’
  52,20,"They will be comfortably reclining on couches arranged in rows, and We will marry them to beautiful maidens with dazzling eyes."
  52,21,"The believers and their descendants who followed them in faith, We shall make their offspring join them (by elevating them to their rank). And We will not reduce anything from (the reward of) their deeds. Every person will be held in pledge for what he has earned."
  52,22,"We will provide them with fruit and meat, as they desire."
  52,23,"There, they will pass a cup (of pure wine) to each other, (and) there will be neither any foolish talk nor sinful speech."
  52,24,And their (attendant) youths will go around them as if they were hidden pearls.
  52,25,"Some of them will advance towards others, questioning each other."
  52,26,"They will say: ‘Before this (blessing), we used to be apprehensive about our families."
  52,27,But Allah showed us (His) favour and protected us from the punishment of the burning heat (of Hell).
  52,28,"Indeed, we used to supplicate Him before. Indeed, He is the Most-Gracious, the All-Merciful.’"
  52,29,"So, (O Prophet!) continue to remind (them). By the grace of your Lord, you are neither a fortune-teller nor a madman."
  52,30,"Or do they say: ‘(He is) a poet, for whom we (eagerly) await a misfortune of time?”"
  52,31,Say: ‘Wait! For I am also waiting with you.’
